      "MISSION 1: Undercover at Bouzoukia in Piraeus\nCategory: Infiltration & Espionage\n\nPublic description to show in mission selection:\nGather intel on a mob boss using a bouzoukia as a front for money laundering.\n\nPRIVATE GM DOSSIER (never reveal to the player)\n\nFixed spatial layout:\nStreet entrance -> narrow foyer and cloakroom -> long former-cinema table\nhall. The stage occupies the far end, a bar runs along one side wall, and a\nrear stair beside the stage climbs to dressing rooms and a small accounting\noffice. A shallow VIP balcony above the foyer overlooks the length of the hall;\na short balcony stair returns to the foyer end of the hall, and the balcony\nhas no backstage connection.\n\nStanding roles, positions, and routines:\nThe boss sits with two associates in the VIP balcony. Accountant Irini is\ncurrently with them while her phone charges in the accounting office. At the\nnext performer change she uses the balcony stair, crosses the hall and climbs\nthe rear stair to collect the phone and check the booking drawer, then returns\nby the same route. The floor\nmanager patrols the central aisle, while ordinary performers and staff use the\nrear stair.\n\nPersistent causal rules:\nIrini's phone holds a voice note in which the boss names the shell-company\ndeposit account, approves the amount and names the next cash pickup. A carbon\nbooking slip in the office drawer carries the matching amount and VIP balcony\ntable code. The\nvoice note remains on the phone and the slip remains in the drawer until\nphysically moved; neither is duplicated elsewhere in the venue.\n\nResolution boundaries:\nFull success preserves the voice note and matching booking slip, or otherwise\ndurably records both so the boss, amount and shell account are linked, while\nthe undercover access remains intact. Partial success secures only one side of\nthe pair, or preserves the full evidence pair at the cost of burning the\ncover. Failure ends access before either side survives in usable form and\nleaves the remaining evidence beyond credible recovery.\n\nPressure and continuity:\nTrack Irini's position, the next performer change, access to the rear stair,\nphone custody, slip custody and social suspicion around the narrow hall and\nrear stair.\n\nFIXED MISSION FACTS\n\nPrepared situation:\nThe laundering is hidden inside inflated private-booking settlements. Irini\nis on the VIP balcony while her phone charges in the accounting office; the\ncarbon slip remains in the lower drawer of the accounting-office desk.\n\nObjective, evidence, custody, and decisive placement:\n- Irini's charging phone in the accounting office contains the boss's voice\n  note naming the shell-company deposit account, approving its amount and\n  naming the next pickup.\n- The carbon booking slip in the lower drawer of the accounting-office desk\n  carries the same amount and the VIP balcony table code.\n\nWhat must be accomplished:\nSecure or durably copy the phone evidence and its matching booking record\nwhile keeping the undercover approach intact.\n\nUseful lead or workable leverage:\nIrini leaves the phone charging through the current loud part of the set and\nreturns to the office at the next performer change.\n\nLive danger:\nStaff using the narrow rear stair recognize one another; an unfamiliar person\nmet there draws immediate attention.\n\nMisleading, partial, or irrelevant elements:\n- The balcony's champagne receipts are genuine patron spending and do not\n  establish laundering.\n\nBinding spatial, custody, and parallel conditions:\nThe accounting-office door is pulled almost closed but not latched. The rear\nstair is dark above the first landing, and the charging phone is not visible\nfrom the hall below.\n\nLater consequences; apply only when their cause occurs:\n- At the next performer change, Irini leaves the VIP balcony by its stair,\n  crosses the hall, climbs the rear stair, enters the accounting office,\n  checks the booking drawer, unplugs the phone and carries it back to the\n  balcony by the same route.\n- If she discovers the phone or booking slip missing during that visit, she\n  returns to the balcony and quietly warns the boss.\n\nOperational facts:\n- The phone and booking slip begin in separate places inside the accounting\n  office.\n- The VIP balcony stair returns only to the foyer end of the public hall.",
