      "MISSION 1: Undercover at Bouzoukia in Piraeus\nCategory: Infiltration & Espionage\n\nPublic description to show in mission selection:\nGather intel on a mob boss using a bouzoukia as a front for money laundering.\n\nPRIVATE GM DOSSIER (never reveal to the player)\n\nFixed spatial layout:\nStreet lobby -> broad stair down -> low-ceiling basement bouzoukia. The main\nroom has a front stage, central tables and a service bar along the rear wall;\na fixed service tablet faces the staff side of that bar. A short staff corridor\nbehind the bar reaches the kitchen, dressing rooms and a staff stair up to a\nloading bay. A rear booth beside the stage has a clear view of the service bar\nbut not the staff stair.\n\nStanding roles, positions, and routines:\nThe boss occupies the rear booth. A new courier waits at the service bar and\nhas been told to follow a reversed flower tray to the boss. A waiter works\nbetween the service bar and table floor and knows the same handoff code, and\none undercover police contact sits conspicuously near the stage. The floor\nmanager controls the staff corridor.\n\nPersistent causal rules:\nBefore the current song ends, the waiter reverses the next flower tray at the\nservice bar and carries it along the main-room aisle to the rear booth. The\ncourier follows the reversed tray from the service bar to the booth. With the\nwaiter still present, the boss gives the pickup address verbally. The waiter\nreturns to the service bar\nand immediately enters the matching coded order on the service tablet. The\ncourier then leaves rear booth -> main room -> broad public stair -> street\nlobby. The police contact has no secret evidence and becomes dangerous only\nif panic exposes the operation.\n\nResolution boundaries:\nFull success identifies the courier and preserves the boss's spoken\ninstruction together with the matching tablet entry, or a durable recording\nof that same exchange that directly links boss, courier and pickup address,\nwhile the undercover\naccess remains intact. Partial success preserves only the courier's identity, only the spoken\ninstruction, or only the coded tablet entry, or preserves the full chain at\nthe cost of burning the cover. Failure ends access with\nneither the courier's identity nor usable boss-linked instruction/tablet\nevidence preserved, and no credible remaining way to recover either.\n\nPressure and continuity:\nTrack the current song, the courier's position, the reversed tray, the pending\nor completed service-tablet entry, the boss's booth and the police contact's\ncomposure. The basement layout keeps exits finite and social mistakes visible\nat close range.\n\nFIXED MISSION FACTS\n\nPrepared situation:\nThe visible envelopes around the tables are theater used to vet the new\ncourier. The real handoff has not yet occurred: before the current song ends,\nthe reversed tray will bring the courier to the boss for a spoken pickup\naddress, followed by one matching coded service-tablet entry.\n\nObjective, evidence, custody, and decisive placement:\n- The new courier begins at the service bar and has not yet received the pickup\n  address.\n- The waiter carries the reversed flower tray from the service bar to the rear\n  booth; the courier follows it to the boss.\n- With the waiter still present at the booth, the boss supplies the pickup\n  address; the waiter then returns to the service bar and enters the matching\n  coded order on the tablet.\n- The courier then leaves by the public stair and street lobby route.\n\nWhat must be accomplished:\nIdentify the courier and preserve the boss-linked spoken instruction together\nwith its matching service-tablet entry, or a durable recording of that same\nexchange directly linking boss, courier and pickup address, while keeping the\nundercover access intact.\n\nUseful lead or workable leverage:\nA flower tray moving against the normal service direction toward the rear\nbooth.\n\nLive danger:\nThe police contact is visibly overplaying confidence and can draw attention if\nchallenged.\n\nMisleading, partial, or irrelevant elements:\n- Cash envelopes displayed at two tables are part of the courier-vetting\n  performance and are not the laundering proof.\n\nBinding spatial, custody, and parallel conditions:\nThe rear booth is partly screened by a column from the public stair, while the\nservice bar and the main-room aisle between bar and booth remain visible from\nthe center tables.\n\nLater consequences; apply only when their cause occurs:\n- If the police contact panics after being directly challenged, the floor\n  manager notices the table before any violence begins.\n- After the waiter enters the coded order, the courier crosses the main room,\n  climbs the broad public stair and leaves through the street lobby; the coded\n  tablet entry remains at the service bar unless physically altered.\n\nOperational facts:\n- The coded tablet entry is created only after the reversed tray and spoken\n  instruction occur.\n- The loading-bay stair is staff access, not the courier's normal departure\n  route.",
