      "MISSION 1: Undercover at Bouzoukia in Piraeus\nCategory: Infiltration & Espionage\n\nPublic description to show in mission selection:\nGather intel on a mob boss using a bouzoukia as a front for money laundering.\n\nPRIVATE GM DOSSIER (never reveal to the player)\n\nFixed spatial layout:\nParking forecourt -> wide ground-floor bouzoukia inside a converted port-side\nhall. A central table floor faces the stage; the flower station and bar sit on\nopposite side walls. A broad backstage opening beside the stage leads to\ndressing rooms, instrument storage and a loading corridor ending at a rear\nservice yard. The manager office opens directly from the main floor beside\nthe bar and overlooks the hall through wired glass.\n\nStanding roles, positions, and routines:\nThe boss sits in side banquette B-6 with a view across the central floor; a\nsmall brass service clip on the banquette edge is stamped B-6. Manolis moves\nbetween the flower station and backstage. The floor manager uses the wired-\nglass office, and stage staff pass regularly through instrument storage. A\nfolded laundering receipt begins beneath a black bouzouki case in the storage\nroom.\n\nPersistent causal rules:\nThe folded receipt names a shell company, deposit account, dated amount and\ntable code B-6. It remains beneath the black instrument case until physically\nmoved. An unstable electrical feed causes one brief dip during the current set,\nlowering stage and hall lighting for a few seconds; emergency strips stay lit\nand staff continue their existing movements.\n\nResolution boundaries:\nFull success preserves the receipt or a durable copy of its contents,\ntogether with a reliable record that B-6 is the boss's banquette, while the\nundercover access remains intact. Partial success preserves the receipt\ncontents without a reliable boss link, or preserves the full evidence at the\ncost of burning the cover. Failure leaves the receipt contents unpreserved and\nthe receipt beyond credible recovery.\n\nPressure and continuity:\nTrack receipt custody, the boss's B-6 banquette, the floor manager's\nwired-glass sightline and the changing visibility between the main floor and\nbackstage.\n\nFIXED MISSION FACTS\n\nPrepared situation:\nThe laundering evidence is a folded settlement receipt under an instrument\ncase backstage, not money in the bar till. The receipt carries table code B-6;\nthe boss is seated at B-6 beside a brass service clip bearing the same code.\nDuring a brief electrical dip, hall and stage lighting falls for a few seconds\nwhile the loading-corridor emergency strips remain lit.\n\nObjective, evidence, custody, and decisive placement:\n- The folded receipt beneath the black bouzouki case names the shell company,\n  deposit account, dated amount and table code B-6.\n- The boss occupies banquette B-6, whose brass service clip visibly carries\n  the same B-6 code.\n\nWhat must be accomplished:\nSecure or durably copy the receipt and preserve a reliable record linking its\nB-6 table code to the boss while keeping the undercover access intact.\n\nUseful lead or workable leverage:\nThe brass service clip at the boss's banquette shows B-6 in the same format as\nthe table code printed on the backstage settlement receipt.\n\nLive danger:\nThe floor manager can see much of the broad hall through the wired-glass\noffice and notices repeated unexplained crossings into backstage.\n\nMisleading, partial, or irrelevant elements:\n- The bar till contains only normal cash sales and performer tips.\n\nBinding spatial, custody, and parallel conditions:\nStage lighting is bright while the outer table floor remains relatively dim.\nThe wired-glass office reflects the stage, reducing its view of one side of\nthe backstage opening.\n\nLater consequences; apply only when their cause occurs:\n- If the boss calls Manolis to B-6 and tells him to bring the settlement\n  receipt, Manolis leaves B-6 -> central floor -> backstage opening ->\n  instrument storage, lifts the black case, pockets the receipt, then returns\n  instrument storage -> backstage opening -> central floor -> B-6.\n- When power stabilizes after a lighting dip, normal hall and stage lighting\n  returns; door locks do not cycle and the instrument cases remain in place.\n\nOperational facts:\n- The receipt begins beneath the black bouzouki case and moves only through\n  physical handling.\n- The rear service yard can be reached only through the loading corridor from\n  backstage.",
