      "MISSION 1: Trap Music Group in Sourmena\nCategory: Infiltration & Espionage\n\nPublic description to show in mission selection:\nInfiltrate a rising Trap music group in Sourmena that is involved in organized crime.\n\nPRIVATE GM DOSSIER (never reveal to the player)\n\nFixed spatial layout:\nA ground-floor rehearsal and video room in Sourmena: street door -> open rehearsal floor -> camera corner and low control desk. A curtained vocal nook occupies one side; a foam-lined wall cabinet and small toilet corridor sit at the rear. The foam cabinet is reachable only from the rehearsal floor and is visible from the camera corner. The street door is the room's only exterior exit.\n\nStanding roles, positions, and routines:\nThree members of the trap group are shooting a simple performance clip; the producer runs playback from the low control desk; a freelance camera operator stays with the camera gear and knows nothing about the criminal business. No criminal handler is on site.\n\nPersistent causal rules:\nA prepaid phone taped behind a removable acoustic panel contains messages assigning collection addresses and amounts. The phone remains fixed behind the panel until moved. The camera operator and ordinary crew phones contain no equivalent record.\n\nResolution boundaries:\nFull success secures or credibly copies the prepaid phone’s message history with attribution to the group. Partial success identifies the phone or records fragments but leaves attribution weak. Failure leaves no usable attributable copy after the phone’s data is destroyed or the phone passes beyond credible recovery.\n\nPressure and continuity:\nTrack clip takes, who has sight of the foam wall, playback pauses and prepaid-phone custody. The camera records only its actual frame; the foam cabinet can remain outside that frame while still visible to people in the room.\n\nFIXED MISSION FACTS\n\nPrepared situation:\nThe group is filming repeated takes against the foam wall. The hidden phone vibrates only when a collection update arrives, producing a faint buzz against the panel during quiet resets.\n\nObjective, evidence, custody, and decisive placement:\n- The prepaid phone behind the foam panel contains the collection instructions.\n\nWhat must be accomplished:\nObtain attributable message evidence tying the collection instructions to the group.\n\nUseful lead or workable leverage:\nA brief vibration comes from inside the foam wall after every ordinary visible phone has stopped ringing.\n\nLive danger:\nAt wrap, the producer removes the hidden phone from the panel, puts it in the control-desk bag and heads for the street door.\n\nMisleading, partial, or irrelevant elements:\n- The camera operator’s equipment cases contain ordinary lenses, batteries and media cards.\n\nBinding spatial, custody, and parallel conditions:\nA take is underway with the performers facing the camera corner; the producer watches playback from the low desk, leaving the rear foam cabinet outside the camera frame but still visible to him.\n\nLater consequences; apply only when their cause occurs:\n- When the shoot wraps, the producer removes the prepaid phone from behind the panel, puts it in the control-desk bag, crosses the rehearsal floor and exits through the street door.\n- If the foam panel is visibly disturbed, the producer checks the hiding place at the next quiet reset.\n",
