      "MISSION 1: Mythical Miniature Retrieval\nCategory: Infiltration & Espionage\n\nPublic description to show in mission selection:\nRetrieve a stolen miniature of Mount Hymettus with supernatural properties from a\nprivate collector's secured villa in Voula. The miniature, created by a genius artist\nliving in Ilioupoli, induces hallucinations tied to Ancient Greek mythology and\ntragedies, causing physical harm to those affected. Infiltrate the villa, bypass its\nadvanced security, and recover the miniature. Return it to the artist's house near\nMount Hymettus in Ilioupoli, where he plans to store it in a secure and undisclosed\nlocation to prevent future theft.\n\nPRIVATE GM DOSSIER (never reveal to the player)\nFixed spatial layout:\nThe Voula villa uses the same secured gate and garden, but the collector has converted a sea-facing library into a private viewing room. The library connects the main hall to a small study and locked cabinet alcove; a service stair from the kitchen reaches the same hall from behind. The pool terrace is outside the library windows but not connected to the cabinet alcove. The Ilioupoli destination remains a separate return leg.\n\nStanding roles, positions, and routines:\nThe collector is actively using the miniature with two invited acquaintances in the library. One guard remains near the front hall and one patrols the garden. A housekeeper works the kitchen and service stair. The guests are not conspirators; they believe they are attending an eccentric private viewing. The artist waits in Ilioupoli.\n\nPersistent causal rules:\nThe collector has become dependent on the miniature's visions and has the object outside its fitted case on a low library table. Each active viewing interval lasts ten minutes. At the end of an interval he carries the miniature to the cabinet alcove, places it inside the fitted containment case and closes the case for a two-minute break; he then reopens it and returns the miniature to the table. The guests' exposure is already causing misrecognition and rising aggression. During the collector's normal cycle the object moves only between the library table and the fitted case in the cabinet alcove.\n\nResolution boundaries:\nFull success removes the miniature from the active viewing, gets it out of the villa inside the fitted case and seals it inside the artist's prepared containment room in Ilioupoli. Partial success delivers the miniature but without the fitted case, with containment badly compromised, or after a serious exposure injury during the transfer. Failure leaves the miniature secured under collector or security control beyond credible recovery, loses it beyond credible recovery during a hallucination, or leaves the player unable to complete delivery.\n\nPressure and continuity:\nTrack the six minutes remaining in the current viewing interval, the two-minute cabinet break, guest exposure, guard positions, cabinet key custody and extraction. The guests can become physically aggressive while the miniature remains exposed; figures perceived in the visions have no physical bodies.\n\nPrepared situation:\nThe private viewing is already underway. The miniature is uncovered on the library table. The library mantel clock reads 21:14; the current ten-minute viewing interval ends at 21:20. One guest is euphoric; the other has begun addressing the collector as a tragic king and is becoming frightened.\n\nObjective, evidence, custody, and decisive placement:\n- The miniature starts uncovered on the library table.\n- The lacquered cabinet alcove contains its fitted containment case.\n- The collector personally controls the cabinet key.\n\nWhat must be accomplished:\nEnd the collector's active use, take the real miniature under containment, escape the villa and return it to the artist in Ilioupoli.\n\nUseful lead or workable leverage:\nIncense resin on the collector's key matches residue around the lacquered cabinet that holds the fitted case.\n\nLive danger:\nThe guests' hallucinations are already escalating into physical misrecognition, making a quiet theft harder the longer the viewing continues.\n\nMisleading, partial, or irrelevant elements:\n- The collector's study contains extensive mythology notes but no second supernatural object.\n- One guest's medication in a handbag is legitimate and unrelated to the visions.\n\nBinding spatial, custody, and parallel conditions:\nOne invited guest has left a coat across the library side chair, narrowing the quiet route to the cabinet alcove without blocking it.\n\nLater consequences; apply only when their cause occurs:\n- At 21:20, if the miniature remains in the collector's custody, he carries it from the library table to the cabinet alcove, places it inside the fitted case and closes it for two minutes.\n- At 21:22, if the miniature remains in his custody, he reopens the fitted case and returns it to the library table.\n- If a guest becomes physically dangerous, the front-hall guard enters the library after hearing a real disturbance.\n- Once the miniature is sealed away from the active viewing, new hallucination escalation stops; injuries already sustained remain.\n\n",
