      "MISSION 1: Syntagma Campaign Sabotage\nCategory: Infiltration & Espionage\n\nPublic description to show in mission selection:\nSabotage a corrupt politician's campaign headquarters near Syntagma.\n\nPRIVATE GM DOSSIER (never reveal to the player)\n\nFixed spatial layout:\nStreet -> campaign reception -> open volunteer hall. The hall connects a media room, phone-bank room and small server/IT closet. A corridor beyond the media room reaches the candidate office and staff exit. The phone-bank room has no independent exterior door.\n\nStanding roles, positions, and routines:\nVolunteers run calls in the phone-bank room. The campaign data manager is at the IT-closet server console with one hardware authorization token on a lanyard. A senior aide works between the media room and candidate office. The outside SMS vendor is remote and receives nothing until the headquarters server completes an authorized transmission.\n\nPersistent causal rules:\nThe corrupt campaign is about to send a mass targeting operation built from unlawfully acquired voter data. The authoritative send list is on the IT-closet server and the physical authorization token is in the data manager's custody. An encrypted export from that server is already running. Volunteer laptops hold only working subsets and cannot authorize the full send. The vendor receives the final package only after the export finishes and the manager confirms it with the token at the server console.\n\nResolution boundaries:\nFull success prevents the current illegal targeting operation from executing in its scheduled send window by compromising the authoritative list, export or token authorization, without revealing the player before the sabotage takes effect. Partial success delays the send or secures proof of the illegal dataset while the intact authoritative list and token remain capable of a later send. Failure occurs when the intact authorized package reaches the outside vendor and becomes executable beyond headquarters control with no proof secured, or when the operation is exposed before any meaningful sabotage or evidence gain.\n\nPressure and continuity:\nTrack the data manager, token custody, the running export and vendor handoff. The export is already in its final phase. When it completes, the data manager begins token confirmation at the same server console; once that brief confirmation completes uninterrupted, the encrypted package transmits to the outside vendor.\n\nFIXED MISSION FACTS\n\nPrepared situation:\nThe campaign headquarters is in an ordinary phone-bank push. The illegal element is hidden inside the final targeting file, not in the volunteers' call scripts. The encrypted export is already in its final phase, and the data manager is at the IT-closet server console with the hardware token on a lanyard.\n\nObjective, evidence, custody, and decisive placement:\n- The authoritative targeting list and running export start on the server in the IT closet.\n- The hardware authorization token starts on the data manager's lanyard.\n- Volunteer laptops contain working subsets but cannot authorize the mass send.\n\nWhat must be accomplished:\nCompromise the campaign's actual illegal targeting send from inside headquarters before the authorized package reaches the outside vendor.\n\nUseful lead or workable leverage:\nPrinted call sheets contain ordinary names, while a data-manager checklist refers to an encrypted 'full universe' export and a token confirmation that volunteers never use.\n\nLive danger:\nSabotaging visible phone-bank machines can cause immediate suspicion while leaving the real server package untouched.\n\nMisleading, partial, or irrelevant elements:\n- A locked drawer near the media room contains only donor wristbands, spare lanyards and merchandise inventory cards.\n- A volunteer complaining about a broken laptop is unrelated to the illegal list.\n\nBinding spatial, custody, and parallel conditions:\nHalf the phone-bank desks are occupied and the two seats nearest the IT-closet aisle are empty; a printed rotation sheet shows the next desk change later.\n\nLater consequences; apply only when their cause occurs:\n- When the export completes, the data manager uses the lanyard token at the IT-closet server console.\n- After the token confirmation completes uninterrupted, the headquarters server transmits the encrypted package to the outside vendor; changes to volunteer laptops no longer affect that transmitted package.",
