      "MISSION 1: Undercover Hooligan Cell in Agios Dimitrios\nCategory: Infiltration & Espionage\n\nPublic description to show in mission selection:\nUndercover as a fan, infiltrate a group of hooligans in Agios Dimitrios who are planning\na violent clash. Gather intelligence on their plans, gain their trust, and then work\nwith law enforcement to prevent the attack.\n\nPRIVATE GM DOSSIER (never reveal to the player)\n\nFixed spatial layout:\nThe cell uses a narrow sports-betting shop as its public meeting point; a rear office\nopens into a covered parking court. A vehicle gate from the court opens onto a side\nstreet. From there one road route leads toward a noisy rendezvous near a metro approach,\nwhile a different road route reaches the rival group's small clubhouse several blocks\naway. A pedestrian lane connects the two destination areas. Two cars and three scooters\nwait in the parking court.\n\nStanding roles, positions, and routines:\nThe visible leader commands five main-group members, including the experienced member\nwho knows both assignments. That arm uses the silver car and all three scooters for the\nmetro-side confrontation. A hardline lieutenant commands two accomplices in the dark\nhatchback for the separate clubhouse raid. The experienced member carries the only\ncomplete vehicle list on a phone. A betting-shop clerk is uninvolved.\n\nPersistent causal rules:\nThe public clash is a diversion. The leader genuinely intends a violent confrontation\nnear the metro, while the lieutenant uses the same period to attack the rival clubhouse\nand destroy property. The hardline hatchback is scheduled to leave first at 23:20; the\nleader's silver car and three scooters leave at 23:30. The two operations do not share\nvehicles. Preventing only the visible clash leaves the second attack intact.\n\nResolution boundaries:\nFull success identifies both attack arms and gets enough concrete information to law\nenforcement for both to be stopped before violent contact. Partial success stops one arm\nwhile the other reaches its target, or preserves actionable identification after some\nviolence has already occurred. Failure lets both attacks make violent contact without a\nusable preventive response, or follows player action that materially enables violent contact by either crew.\n\nPressure and continuity:\nTrack main-group trust, lieutenant suspicion, the 23:20 and 23:30 departures and the\nplayer's communication channel to police. The two arms continue on their own routes once\nthey leave the parking court.\n\nFIXED MISSION FACTS\n\nPrepared situation:\nThe leader is openly discussing the metro rendezvous. The lieutenant carries a vehicle-\ninsurance sleeve in his jacket with the clubhouse route card folded inside. The\nexperienced member's phone holds a photograph of a handwritten page listing all five\nvehicle assignments and both departure times.\n\nObjective, evidence, custody, and decisive placement:\n- The leader's arm uses the silver car and three scooters for the metro-side rendezvous\n at 23:30.\n- The lieutenant and two accomplices use the dark hatchback for the clubhouse raid at\n 23:20; the lieutenant carries the route card inside the insurance sleeve in his jacket.\n- The experienced member's phone holds the only single image listing all five vehicle\n assignments, both targets and both departure times.\n\nWhat must be accomplished:\nDiscover that the planned violence has two coordinated targets and pass enough concrete\ndetail for both attacks to be intercepted before contact.\n\nUseful lead or workable leverage:\nThe lieutenant's car is loaded with a crowbar and paint thinner that make little sense\nfor the announced face-to-face clash but fit a property raid.\n\nLive danger:\nPolice action against the obvious crowd can unintentionally free the smaller car crew to\nleave unnoticed if the split plan has not been identified.\n\nMisleading, partial, or irrelevant elements:\n- The betting-shop clerk knows members by nickname but has no operational role.\n- A loud argument over football predictions is genuine social noise, not a coded\n instruction.\n\nBinding spatial, custody, and parallel conditions:\nA routine customer dispute keeps the betting-shop clerk and two members at the front\ncounter, leaving the rear office socially thinner while the parking court remains\noccupied.\n\nLater consequences; apply only when their cause occurs:\n- At 23:20 the lieutenant and two accomplices leave the parking court in the dark\n hatchback, pass through the vehicle gate and take the clubhouse road unless stopped.\n- At 23:30 the leader and five main-group members leave in the silver car and three\n scooters through the same gate, then take the metro-side road unless stopped.\n- Police told about only one arm position against only that identified threat until\n further information reaches them.",
