      "MISSION 1: Kifissia High-End Club Front\n  Category: Infiltration & Espionage\n\n  Public description to show in mission selection:\n  A high-end club in Kifissia is rumored to front illicit activity. Infiltrate the venue, plant one supplied listening device beneath the private-mezzanine meeting table, and extract sensitive information that could expose its criminal enterprise.\n\n  PRIVATE GM DOSSIER (never reveal to the player)\n\n  Fixed spatial layout:\nThe club occupies the first floor of a modern commercial building on Kifisias Avenue. A street-level entrance lobby with door staff leads by stair and lift to the main club floor: long bar -> compact dance floor -> rear double-height lounge. A private mezzanine runs above one side of the rear lounge and contains the required central meeting table behind a slatted-glass screen. Behind the bar, a staff corridor reaches the manager/security office and a service stair down to a rear service lane that joins a side street. The mezzanine has a guarded VIP stair from the lounge and a staff stair from the corridor; neither route bypasses the first-floor club entirely.\n\n  Standing roles, positions, and routines:\nA corrupt regulatory official is meeting two criminal principals on the mezzanine to renew protection for the club's enterprise. The two principals wait in the rear lounge until the official reaches them. The official carries a slim briefcase. A security technician sweeps the mezzanine table and screened seating area once before the meeting, then returns to the manager/security office. The club host circulates between the main bar and rear lounge. Door staff control the street lobby and keep a simple VIP arrival sheet. The official's chauffeur waits with a sedan on a nearby side street and approaches the entrance only when called.\n\n  Resolution boundaries:\n  Full success requires a working listening tag concealed beneath the mezzanine table after the security sweep and the protection evidence from the official's briefcase or a faithful copy secured without attribution. Partial success completes only one objective, or completes both after the intrusion becomes attributable. Failure occurs only when the table remains untagged and no protection evidence or faithful copy has been preserved after the official passes beyond credible recovery, or the player is captured/incapacitated before either objective is secured.\n\n  Pressure and continuity:\nTrack the scheduled security sweep, the official's briefcase custody, the chauffeur's pickup and street-lobby suspicion. The technician completes one physical sweep fifteen minutes before the official sits. The official keeps the briefcase in hand from the street lobby to the mezzanine, places it beside the meeting chair during talks, then carries it back downstairs. The chauffeur approaches only after receiving the official's call.\n\n  FIXED MISSION FACTS\n\n  Prepared situation:\nTonight is not a routine club meeting but a protection renewal conducted during normal high-end nightlife. The official's briefcase contains signed inspection waivers and a burner phone used to coordinate prior warnings. The security technician inspects the table underside and screened seating area before the meeting; anything fixed beneath the table before that sweep is exposed to that inspection.\n\n  Objective, evidence, custody, and decisive placement:\n- The supplied listening tag must end beneath the central mezzanine meeting table after the sweep.\n- The official enters through the street lobby with the briefcase in hand. Inside are two signed waiver copies and one burner phone.\n- During the meeting the briefcase rests beside the official's chair, still within arm's reach; no staff member takes custody.\n- The VIP arrival sheet at the street lobby proves the official's presence but not the criminal agreement by itself.\n\n  What must be accomplished:\n  Have the working tag concealed beneath the mezzanine table after the security sweep and secure evidence that ties the official to the protection arrangement before the official and briefcase pass beyond credible recovery.\n\n  Useful lead or workable leverage:\n  The technician carries a compact inspection mirror and kneels beneath the mezzanine table during the pre-meeting sweep, making the timing of the clean table state observable.\n\n  Live danger:\n  The official's security status lets a minor social suspicion trigger an immediate identity check by door or club staff.\n\n  Misleading, partial, or irrelevant elements:\n- The street-lobby VIP arrival sheet is accurate but insufficient on its own.\n- A separately locked cabinet behind the main bar contains rare spirits and private bottles rather than hidden documents.\n\n  Binding spatial, custody, and parallel conditions:\nThe security technician is in the manager/security office checking the sweep kit. The corrupt official has not arrived; the host is receiving members on the first-floor main bar and rear lounge, and the mezzanine remains unused.\n\n  Later consequences; apply only when their cause occurs:\n- When the sweep is completed, the technician reports the table clean and returns to the manager/security office.\n- At the end of the meeting, the official calls the chauffeur while carrying the briefcase back through the club to the street entrance. The chauffeur brings the sedan from the nearby side street, picks up the official, and departs with any evidence still in the briefcase.",
