      "MISSION 1: Kifissia High-End Club Front\n  Category: Infiltration & Espionage\n\n  Public description to show in mission selection:\n  A high-end club in Kifissia is rumored to front illicit activity. Infiltrate the venue, plant one supplied listening device beneath the private-mezzanine meeting table, and extract sensitive information that could expose its criminal enterprise.\n\n  PRIVATE GM DOSSIER (never reveal to the player)\n\n  Fixed spatial layout:\n  The club uses a restaurant front over a basement after-hours room. Street foyer -> restaurant/bar -> public stair down to the basement club floor. A short guarded stair rises from the club floor to a bridge-like private mezzanine holding the required meeting table. Behind the basement bar, a service lift links the manager office to an underground garage. Staff lockers and a stock room sit off the office corridor. A gated vehicle ramp connects the underground garage to a side street. The public stair and service lift are the only routes between the restaurant level and the lower operational spaces; the short mezzanine stair serves only the bridge level.\n\n  Standing roles, positions, and routines:\n  The criminal principals suspect an internal leak and are conducting one final emergency meeting on the mezzanine before moving records out. The manager remains with the encrypted accounts laptop in the office until the ledger copy completes. A bookkeeper copies its active ledger to a portable SSD. Before last admission closes, one security staffer holds the street foyer while the other circulates the basement club floor; afterward they clear the public areas in that same outward-to-lower sequence. A driver waits beside a dark sedan in the underground garage for the laptop and SSD and holds the remote for the gated vehicle ramp.\n\n  Resolution boundaries:\n  Full success requires the listening tag beneath the mezzanine table and the active account ledger secured from the laptop/SSD without leaving a conclusive identity trail. Partial success completes only one objective, secures an incomplete ledger, or completes both after the intrusion becomes attributable. Failure occurs only when the table remains untagged and no usable ledger copy is preserved after the laptop and SSD pass beyond credible recovery, or the player is captured/incapacitated before either objective is secured.\n\n  Pressure and continuity:\n  The shutdown has four concrete stages: last admission, public-floor thinning, ledger copy completion, garage departure. The bookkeeper begins copying only after the principals enter the mezzanine. When the copy reaches completion, the SSD moves from bookkeeper to manager; the manager carries laptop and SSD by service lift to the garage and hands both to the waiting driver. Security closes the restaurant entrance only after the last announced drink unless a concrete disturbance changes the shutdown routine.\n\n  FIXED MISSION FACTS\n\n  Prepared situation:\n  Someone inside the enterprise has warned the principals that records are vulnerable. The warning concerns an internal leak, and the principals are quietly collapsing the night's operation while keeping the club outwardly normal. The final mezzanine meeting decides what gets abandoned, and the live account ledger is being prepared for removal in the office below.\n\n  Objective, evidence, custody, and decisive placement:\n  - The supplied tag must be installed beneath the bridge-mezzanine meeting table.\n- The encrypted accounts laptop begins open in the manager office under the manager's control.\n- The bookkeeper carries the portable SSD; it remains blank until the principals take their seats, then begins receiving the active-ledger copy.\n- At copy completion, the SSD transfers to the manager; the manager carries both devices by service lift to the underground garage and hands them to the driver beside the dark sedan.\n\n  What must be accomplished:\n  Plant the working listening tag beneath the private-mezzanine table and secure the active account information before its named custody chain carries the evidence beyond credible recovery.\n\n  Useful lead or workable leverage:\n  The bookkeeper is the only staff member repeatedly checking both the office laptop and the service-lift indicator instead of the club floor.\n\n  Live danger:\n  During closure, one security staffer works down from the restaurant toward the public stair while the other clears the basement club floor, concentrating observation around the public stair and the office-side route to the service lift.\n\n  Misleading, partial, or irrelevant elements:\n  - Shredded restaurant receipts in a stock-room bin are routine end-of-night waste.\n- A locked staff locker contains undeclared cash tips but no account ledger.\n\n  Binding spatial, custody, and parallel conditions:\n  Last admission is still open and the club looks normal. The accounts laptop is open in the manager office, the blank SSD is in the bookkeeper's pocket, and the principals have not yet gone to the mezzanine.\n\n  Later consequences; apply only when their cause occurs:\n  - When the ledger copy completes, the SSD transfers to the manager. The manager carries laptop and SSD by service lift to the underground garage and hands both to the waiting driver.\n- After receiving the laptop and SSD, the driver opens the gated ramp with the garage remote and leaves in the dark sedan to the side street, carrying any account evidence still on those devices.",
