      "MISSION 1: Kidnapping in Koropi\nCategory: Rescue Missions\n\nPublic description to show in mission selection:\nTrack down and rescue a kidnapped tech entrepreneur being held in a remote farmhouse in\nKoropi. Neutralize the kidnappers and ensure the victim's safety.\n\nPRIVATE GM DOSSIER (never reveal to the player)\n\nFixed spatial layout:\nThe property combines an old farmhouse with a modern produce-packing shed. The rural\nlane reaches a shared yard; one side enters the farmhouse kitchen and bedrooms, while\nthe other enters the packing floor -> wash area -> insulated cold room. A loading bay\nbehind the shed opens onto a short truck apron and the rural lane. A narrow service passage links the packing floor\nto the farmhouse pantry but not to the bedrooms.\n\nStanding roles, positions, and routines:\nThe kidnapping leader stays in the farmhouse handling ransom communications. A\nwarehouse-type accomplice controls the packing shed and cold-room key. The entrepreneur\nis restrained inside the insulated cold room because its walls suppress sound. A third\ncaptor is due to return with the box truck; no one is continuously stationed inside the\ncold room.\n\nPersistent causal rules:\nThe cold room is functioning and the lightly dressed victim is developing dangerous cold\nexposure. The shed captor has the mechanical key; the thermostat in the wash area\ncontrols temperature but does not unlock the door. The returning truck is the planned\nrelocation vehicle and cannot take the victim until it physically reaches the loading\nbay.\n\nResolution boundaries:\nFull success gets the victim out of the cold room, stabilizes them enough for safe\nextraction and prevents the captors from regaining custody. Partial success rescues the\nvictim with serious medical deterioration or loses the ransom/vehicle evidence. Failure\nis lethal cold exposure or the box truck leaving the property with the victim beyond\nimmediate interception.\n\nPressure and continuity:\nTrack cold-room exposure, key custody, thermostat state, truck arrival and loading-bay\naccess. Warming the room slows medical deterioration but also changes compressor noise\nand power draw in a way the shed captor can notice on the next routine check.\n\nFIXED MISSION FACTS\n\nPrepared situation:\nThe victim is conscious but shivering in the locked cold room. The shed captor carries\nthe mechanical key. The box truck is off-site on its return leg; the loading bay is\nempty and closed.\n\nObjective, evidence, custody, and decisive placement:\n- The victim starts inside the insulated cold room on the packing floor.\n- The cold-room mechanical key starts on the shed captor.\n- The box truck starts off-site and becomes a relocation threat only after arriving at\n the rear loading bay.\n\nWhat must be accomplished:\nRelease and medically preserve the entrepreneur, then remove them from the property\nbeyond immediate captor recovery.\n\nUseful lead or workable leverage:\nCondensation around the cold-room frame and a recently removed coat on the packing-floor\nhook indicate a person was put inside without proper cold-weather clothing.\n\nLive danger:\nThe victim has a finite cold-exposure problem; a technically successful door opening can\nstill become a failed rescue if the player forces an exhausting escape without\nstabilization.\n\nMisleading, partial, or irrelevant elements:\n- The farmhouse bedrooms are occupied only by captors' personal effects.\n- The wash-area thermostat changes temperature but is not an electronic door release.\n\nBinding spatial, custody, and parallel conditions:\nThe packing line is washing empty crates, creating floor noise and slick patches between\nthe shed entrance and cold room. The machine cycle ends on a predictable timer.\n\nLater consequences; apply only when their cause occurs:\n- Reducing refrigeration slows the victim's deterioration after the system has actually\n warmed; it does not instantly reverse exposure.\n- When the box truck arrives, the returning captor backs it to the loading bay and joins\n the shed captor. If relocation then begins, they must take the victim from the cold room\n through the wash area and packing floor to the bay, load the truck, and depart by the\n rural lane.\n- Once the victim is outside the cold room, their impaired movement and need for warmth\n remain persistent until treated.",
