      "MISSION 1: Rentis Freight Train Heist\nCategory: Heists & Raids\n\nPublic description to show in mission selection:\nIntercept a freight consist in the Agios Ioannis Rentis rail yard and unload valuable cargo before authorities respond.\n\nPRIVATE GM DOSSIER (never reveal to the player)\n\nFixed spatial layout:\nCheckpoint -> warehouse apron -> freight consist on loading siding. The target curtain-side wagon is aligned with an apron but its palletized electronics sit one meter above road level. A yard forklift is parked inside a caged charging bay beside the warehouse, and the getaway van can reverse to the apron only through a marked vehicle lane. The locomotive end of the siding is fenced from the warehouse yard.\n\nStanding roles, positions, and routines:\nA warehouse supervisor holds the forklift key card, one forklift operator is on meal break, two loaders work the outgoing pallet flow around the apron, and a rail guard remains near the locomotive end. Normal delivery lorries also use the marked vehicle lane and can occupy it briefly during routine paperwork or loading. The getaway driver waits outside the checkpoint until given a clear entry cue.\n\nPersistent causal rules:\nSix palletized cartons of high-value electronics are inside the target wagon and are too heavy for rapid hand unloading. The yard forklift is the practical handling tool; damaging the pallets by dropping or dragging them reduces the job's value. The supervisor's key card activates the forklift, and the vehicle lane must remain clear long enough for the getaway van to load.\n\nResolution boundaries:\nFull success transfers all six contracted pallets into the getaway van in usable condition before response closes the yard. Partial success secures at least one usable contracted pallet but fewer than all six in usable condition, or secures the full load with meaningful damage to part of it. Failure secures no usable contracted pallets before authorities block extraction.\n\nPressure and continuity:\nTrack forklift access, pallet count, supervisor attention, vehicle-lane blockage, getaway-van position and the loading crew's return from break.\n\nFIXED MISSION FACTS\n\nPrepared situation:\nThe target wagon is correctly positioned for unloading, but the valuable electronics are palletized and cannot be removed quickly by hand. The normal forklift operator is on meal break, leaving a short interruption before normal loading resumes.\n\nObjective, evidence, custody, and decisive placement:\n- Six contracted electronics pallets begin inside the target curtain-side wagon.\n- The yard forklift in the charging cage is the only fast local handling equipment suitable for the pallet weight.\n- The warehouse supervisor's key card activates the forklift and starts in the supervisor's possession.\n\nWhat must be accomplished:\nUse or replace the real material-handling capacity to transfer the six contracted pallets into the getaway vehicle before the yard response closes the lane.\n\nUseful lead or workable leverage:\nForklift scuff marks and matching pallet widths show that the same charging-bay machine is used for this wagon's normal unloading.\n\nLive danger:\nA blocked vehicle lane or disabled forklift can strand valuable pallets in the open where they are visible but no longer extractable in time.\n\nMisleading, partial, or irrelevant elements:\n- Smaller cartons stacked near the warehouse door are valuable spare parts but are not part of the contracted shipment.\n\nBinding spatial, custody, and parallel conditions:\nThe forklift is plugged into its charger with enough battery for the full job. The supervisor is inside the warehouse office, while the two loaders are eating near the far end of the apron.\n\nLater consequences; apply only when their cause occurs:\n- When the meal break ends, the forklift operator returns to the charging bay and expects the machine and key card to be present.\n- If the getaway van enters, its position on the marked lane becomes visible to the warehouse supervisor and loaders.\n- Pallets already secured inside the van remain part of the achieved objective even if remaining cargo becomes unreachable.",
