      "MISSION 1: Gero-Thanassis' Secret Recordings Heist\nCategory: Heists & Raids\n\nPublic description to show in mission selection:\nA wealthy music collector has caught wind of a legendary, hidden collection: an\narchive of unreleased 60s and 70s recordings produced by the elusive \"gero-Thanassis,\"\nfeaturing some of the era's most iconic voices and composers. Held in gero-Thanassis'\nold house in Perama, this collection is fiercely guarded by his two great-grandsons,\nTrap artists with little interest in their ancestor's legacy but resolute in honoring\nhis last wish to keep the recordings secret. Your client wants these records at any\ncost, knowing they'll never willingly sell. Your task: infiltrate the Perama home,\navoid (or neutralize) the great-grandsons' suspicions, and retrieve as much of the\ncollection as possible. Deliver the music to the collector's sleek apartment near\nFilopappou without a trace, securing a trove of timeless songs that was almost lost to\nobscurity.\n\nPRIVATE GM DOSSIER (never reveal to the player)\n\nFixed spatial layout:\nStreet -> front room -> hall -> ancestor bedroom, kitchen and rear yard. The trap-studio room opens from the front room. An old hatchback is parked nose-out in the rear yard, reachable only through the kitchen. Three archive boxes are being moved one by one from the ancestor bedroom through the kitchen into the car. The car exits through a narrow side gate to the street.\n\nStanding roles, positions, and routines:\nBoth great-grandsons are home at dawn and are relocating the archive after a rumor about the recordings reached strangers online. One carries boxes from the ancestor bedroom; the other packs the hatchback, watches the side gate and is the car's driver. No buyer is involved: they are moving the collection to keep the ancestor's secret. The Filopappou client knows only the Perama address.\n\nPersistent causal rules:\nThree numbered archive boxes contain the complete target: reels in Box 1, cassettes in Box 2 and session notebooks in Box 3. They move from the ancestor bedroom to the hatchback in numerical order, always through the kitchen and rear yard. Once the third box is loaded, the driver departs through the side gate for private storage outside the mission area unless stopped by events already established in play.\n\nResolution boundaries:\nFull success requires all three archive boxes to reach the Filopappou client intact and untraced. One or two authentic boxes count as partial recovery; all three delivered with an attributable theft trail that stops short of exposing the client before handoff is also partial. Failure follows only when no authentic box can still be delivered because the hatchback has departed with every unrecovered box and any previously secured material has also been lost, or when the client is reliably exposed before handoff.\n\nPressure and continuity:\nTrack each numbered box separately, the kitchen-to-yard carrying route, the side gate, the hatchback's loading state and the delivery leg. The player's opportunity changes because the grandsons are physically moving the archive, not because the world invents a chase.\n\nFIXED MISSION FACTS\n\nPrepared situation:\nAll archive material is still on the Perama property when the player arrives, but the grandsons have decided the address is compromised. Their effort to honor the last wish creates a finite loading operation and turns the home heist into a moving-custody problem without changing the target.\n\nObjective, evidence, custody, and decisive placement:\n- Box 1 contains four master reels; Box 2 contains seven master cassettes; Box 3 contains two further master reels plus the original session notebook that authenticates the full set.\n- The boxes transfer from the ancestor bedroom to the rear-yard hatchback in order: Box 1, then Box 2, then Box 3.\n- The side gate is the hatchback's only exit from the property.\n\nWhat must be accomplished:\nSecure the three-box archive and deliver the recovered authentic recordings to Filopappou; full success requires all three boxes intact and untraced, while a genuine subset remains partial recovery.\n\nUseful lead or workable leverage:\nThree fresh strips of packing tape and numbered cardboard lids sit beside the ancestor-bedroom doorway, while the rear-yard hatchback has its cargo cover already removed.\n\nLive danger:\nEvery completed box transfer puts part of the archive closer to a vehicle departure while keeping both great-grandsons active on the route.\n\nMisleading, partial, or irrelevant elements:\n- A fourth unnumbered carton in the front room contains the great-grandsons' merchandise and cables.\n- The hatchback glove box contains ordinary vehicle papers, not archive records.\n\nBinding spatial, custody, and parallel conditions:\nBox 1 has already been loaded in the rear-yard hatchback; Boxes 2 and 3 remain in the ancestor bedroom. One grandson is returning through the kitchen for Box 2 while the other arranges cargo in the car.\n\nLater consequences; apply only when their cause occurs:\n- Each completed carry moves the next numbered box from the bedroom to the hatchback.\n- After Box 3 is loaded, the hatchback leaves through the side gate unless the established situation prevents departure.",
