      "MISSION 1: Nea Smyrni Safehouse Raid\nCategory: Heists & Raids\n\nPublic description to show in mission selection:\nStorm a hidden safehouse to capture a notorious gang leader.\n\nPRIVATE GM DOSSIER (never reveal to the player)\n\nFixed spatial layout:\nSide street -> small apartment block entrance -> ground-floor safehouse. The\nflat has a front sitting room, central kitchen, rear bedroom and enclosed\ncourtyard. A rear gate from the courtyard opens to a parallel lane. The\nbathroom and utility cupboard are dead ends.\n\nStanding roles, positions, and routines:\nThe real leader begins in the rear bedroom with a bodyguard. A second henchman watches the courtyard from the kitchen. No decoy is present. A pickup car with a dedicated driver is scheduled to stop outside the rear gate after a fixed interval; the driver does not enter the property.\n\nPersistent causal rules:\nThe leader stays in the rear bedroom until warned or until the scheduled pickup arrives. At pickup time the courtyard henchman opens the rear gate, then the leader crosses bedroom -> kitchen -> courtyard -> rear gate to the waiting car. The pickup car does not enter the courtyard; if the leader reaches it, the driver departs with the target unless intercepted.\n\nResolution boundaries:\nFull success captures and controls the real leader before the pickup car gets the target away beyond practical interception. Secondary phones or cash are optional. Partial success leaves the leader gone but secures attributable safehouse evidence. Failure occurs only once the pickup car has carried the leader away beyond practical interception with no equivalent evidence secured.\n\nPressure and continuity:\nTrack the fixed pickup time, rear-gate state, courtyard control, leader position, pickup-car departure and player control of the front entrance. The leader does not move early without warning.\n\nPrepared situation:\nThe target is genuinely inside a modest ground-floor flat, not behind a decoy.\nThe difficulty is the short rear route to a scheduled pickup car that never\nneeds to approach the front of the building.\n\nObjective, evidence, custody, and decisive placement:\n- The real leader begins in the rear bedroom.\n- A rear courtyard gate provides the only direct route to the scheduled pickup\n  on the parallel lane.\n\nWhat must be accomplished:\nCapture the leader before the rear-lane pickup carries the target away beyond practical interception.\n\nUseful lead or workable leverage:\nFresh tire marks on the parallel lane stop directly behind the courtyard gate\nrather than at the building entrance.\n\nLive danger:\nOnce the rear gate opens, the short bedroom-to-courtyard route can put the leader beside the waiting pickup car very quickly.\n\nMisleading, partial, or irrelevant elements:\n- The utility cupboard contains cash boxes but no hidden passage.\n- The front sitting room has a second phone used by a henchman, not the\n  leader.\n\nBinding spatial, custody, and parallel conditions:\nThe rear courtyard gate is closed and locked from inside. The scheduled pickup\nhas not yet reached the parallel lane.\n\nLater consequences; apply only when their cause occurs:\n- At the fixed pickup time the driver stops outside the rear gate, the courtyard henchman opens it and signals the leader.\n- A warned leader uses the same bedroom -> kitchen -> courtyard -> rear gate route before the pickup time.\n- If the leader reaches the pickup car, the driver departs along the parallel lane unless physically prevented or intercepted.\n\nOperational facts:\n- Capturing the leader ends the capture objective even if the pickup car later\n  leaves empty.\n- The rear gate changes state only through physical opening, closing or\n  blocking.",
      "MISSION 1: Nea Smyrni Safehouse Raid\nCategory: Heists & Raids\n\nPublic description to show in mission selection:\nStorm a hidden safehouse to capture a notorious gang leader.\n\nPRIVATE GM DOSSIER (never reveal to the player)\n\nFixed spatial layout:\nSide street -> small apartment block entrance -> ground-floor safehouse. The\nflat has a front sitting room, central kitchen, rear bedroom and enclosed\ncourtyard. A rear gate from the courtyard opens to a parallel lane. The\nbathroom and utility cupboard are dead ends.\n\nStanding roles, positions, and routines:\nThe real leader begins in the rear bedroom with a bodyguard. A second henchman watches the courtyard from the kitchen. No decoy is present. A pickup car with a dedicated driver is scheduled to stop outside the rear gate after a fixed interval; the driver does not enter the property.\n\nPersistent causal rules:\nThe leader stays in the rear bedroom until warned or until the scheduled pickup arrives. At pickup time the courtyard henchman opens the rear gate, then the leader crosses bedroom -> kitchen -> courtyard -> rear gate to the waiting car. The pickup car does not enter the courtyard; if the leader reaches it, the driver departs with the target unless intercepted.\n\nResolution boundaries:\nFull success captures and controls the real leader before the pickup car gets the target away beyond practical interception. Secondary phones or cash are optional. Partial success leaves the leader gone but secures attributable safehouse evidence. Failure occurs only once the pickup car has carried the leader away beyond practical interception with no equivalent evidence secured.\n\nPressure and continuity:\nTrack the fixed pickup time, rear-gate state, courtyard control, leader position, pickup-car departure and player control of the front entrance. The leader does not move early without warning.\n\nPrepared situation:\nThe target is genuinely inside a modest ground-floor flat, not behind a decoy.\nThe difficulty is the short rear route to a scheduled pickup car that never\nneeds to approach the front of the building.\n\nObjective, evidence, custody, and decisive placement:\n- The real leader begins in the rear bedroom.\n- A rear courtyard gate provides the only direct route to the scheduled pickup\n  on the parallel lane.\n\nWhat must be accomplished:\nCapture the leader before the rear-lane pickup carries the target away beyond practical interception.\n\nUseful lead or workable leverage:\nFresh tire marks on the parallel lane stop directly behind the courtyard gate\nrather than at the building entrance.\n\nLive danger:\nOnce the rear gate opens, the short bedroom-to-courtyard route can put the leader beside the waiting pickup car very quickly.\n\nMisleading, partial, or irrelevant elements:\n- The utility cupboard contains cash boxes but no hidden passage.\n- The front sitting room has a second phone used by a henchman, not the\n  leader.\n\nBinding spatial, custody, and parallel conditions:\nThe kitchen door to the courtyard is open, giving the courtyard henchman a\nclear line back toward the rear bedroom corridor while the front sitting room\nremains out of sight.\n\nLater consequences; apply only when their cause occurs:\n- At the fixed pickup time the driver stops outside the rear gate, the courtyard henchman opens it and signals the leader.\n- A warned leader uses the same bedroom -> kitchen -> courtyard -> rear gate route before the pickup time.\n- If the leader reaches the pickup car, the driver departs along the parallel lane unless physically prevented or intercepted.\n\nOperational facts:\n- Capturing the leader ends the capture objective even if the pickup car later\n  leaves empty.\n- The rear gate changes state only through physical opening, closing or\n  blocking.",
