      "MISSION 1: Nea Smyrni Safehouse Raid\nCategory: Heists & Raids\n\nPublic description to show in mission selection:\nStorm a hidden safehouse to capture a notorious gang leader.\n\nPRIVATE GM DOSSIER (never reveal to the player)\n\nFixed spatial layout:\nMain road -> narrow stair door beside a shuttered storefront -> first-floor\nsafehouse. A front lounge opens to a long corridor with kitchenette, bathroom\nand back office. The back office reaches a rear metal stair descending to a\nservice yard. The storefront below is empty and has no internal connection to\nthe flat.\n\nStanding roles, positions, and routines:\nThe gang leader and one lieutenant begin in the back office. An armed guard\nholds the front lounge. No civilians are inside. The leader intends to leave\nthrough the rear metal stair at the end of a fixed meeting interval; the\nlieutenant remains behind.\n\nPersistent causal rules:\nUntil the meeting interval ends or an alarm reaches the back office, the\nleader stays there. Departure follows back office -> rear stair -> service\nyard -> side street. The empty storefront below cannot be entered from the\nsafehouse.\n\nResolution boundaries:\nFull success captures the leader inside the flat or along the established rear route before the target gets clear via the side street. Partial success captures the lieutenant and secures the leader's signed meeting ledger after the leader escapes. Failure occurs once the leader gets clear via the side street with the signed ledger and no equivalent evidence secured.\n\nPressure and continuity:\nTrack meeting time, front-guard alert, rear-stair control, leader custody and\nsigned-ledger custody. The fixed departure is the only scheduled movement.\n\nFIXED MISSION FACTS\n\nPrepared situation:\nThe safehouse is above a dead storefront and easy to misread from the road.\nThe target is already in a quiet meeting at the back, with a real rear stair\nprepared for departure but no elaborate decoy system.\n\nObjective, evidence, custody, and decisive placement:\n- The real leader begins in the back office with a signed meeting ledger on\n  the table.\n- The rear metal stair is the target's established departure route.\n\nWhat must be accomplished:\nCapture the leader before the established back-office -> rear-stair -> service-yard -> side-street departure gets the target clear beyond practical interception; the signed ledger provides a strong partial result only if capture fails.\n\nUseful lead or workable leverage:\nFresh shoe grit runs from the stair door through the corridor toward the back\noffice rather than the empty storefront.\n\nLive danger:\nA warning from the front lounge shortens the time before the leader takes the\nrear metal stair.\n\nMisleading, partial, or irrelevant elements:\n- The shuttered storefront below contains no safehouse access.\n- The lieutenant's phone is ordinary personal traffic and does not substitute\n  for the signed ledger.\n\nBinding spatial, custody, and parallel conditions:\nThe narrow street stair door is scuffed but closed. The front guard is in the\nlounge and the meeting continues in the back office.\n\nLater consequences; apply only when their cause occurs:\n- At the end of the meeting interval the leader takes the ledger and leaves back office -> rear stair -> service yard -> side street, continuing away from the safehouse unless intercepted.\n- A clear alarm reaching the back office causes the same departure to begin early.\n\nOperational facts:\n- Capturing the leader secures the primary objective even if the ledger is\n  destroyed later.\n- The signed ledger stays on the back-office table until the leader or player\n  picks it up.",
