      "MISSION 1: Agia Paraskevi Blueprints\nCategory: Heists & Raids\n\nPublic description to show in mission selection:\nAn innovative architect based in Agia Paraskevi has had crucial blueprints stolen.\nSuspicions point to a jealous rival operating out of Halandri. Infiltrate the rival's\noffice or residence, locate the designs, and retrieve them.\n\nPRIVATE GM DOSSIER (never reveal to the player)\n\nFixed spatial layout:\nActive graph: rival office reception -> shared printer -> dispatch shelf -> staff exit -> ordinary street route -> kiosk counter and outgoing parcel slot. The kiosk slot is accessible to its attendant and the collecting courier. The office safe is a dead end; the Halandri residence is not part of this operation.\n\nStanding roles, positions, and routines:\nThe rival and interns remain at the office. The kiosk attendant controls the parcel slot, and one collecting courier reaches the kiosk after the current pickup route. The originals remain in the sealed kiosk envelope until the attendant or courier physically removes it.\n\nResolution boundaries:\nFull success: authentic originals and the evidence of theft or alteration are recovered and remain deliverable. Partial: usable originals are secured and delivered, but provenance, alteration evidence, or the wider scheme remains unresolved. Failure: the kiosk courier carries the sealed originals beyond practical interception before they are secured, the originals are seized or lost before delivery, or the player is detained with no credible way to deliver the designs or establish provenance.\n\nPressure and continuity:\nTrack the kiosk envelope, office dispatch stub, attendant and courier custody, public visibility, and any police or social heat created by an obvious grab.\n\nFIXED MISSION FACTS\n\nPrepared situation:\nThe originals sit inside the street kiosk's outgoing parcel slot, sealed in an envelope\nidentifiable by its thickness and incorrect stamp. The office safe is bait; taking the\nenvelope openly draws the attendant's attention and creates police and social heat, making\nprovenance and clean delivery harder even if the designs are physically secured.\n\nObjective, evidence, custody, and decisive placement:\n- The originals are sealed in the courier envelope inside the street kiosk's outgoing parcel\n  slot, identifiable by its unusual thickness and wrong stamp.\n\nWhat must be accomplished:\nAuthentic originals and evidence of theft or alteration are recovered.\n\nUseful lead or workable leverage:\nThe wrong stamp repeated on the office dispatch stub.\n\nLive danger:\nRecovering the designs in a way that makes the player appear to be the thief.\n\nMisleading, partial, or irrelevant elements:\n- The office safe is bait.\n\nBinding spatial, custody, and parallel conditions:\nThe dispatch shelf is visible from reception, while the kiosk parcel slot is one ordinary street crossing away and cannot be seen from inside the office. The wrong-stamped envelope remains below the kiosk counter lip until physically removed.\n\nLater consequences; apply only when their cause occurs:\n- If the envelope is grabbed openly, the attendant reacts and police and social heat follow. The designs remain physically secured if the player keeps them, but provenance and delivery become harder.",
