      "MISSION 1: Tourkovounia's Faithful Fire\nCategory: Combat & Defense\n\nPublic description to show in mission selection:\nA radical neo-Orthodox armed faction has established a fortified encampment atop the Tourkovounia hills, stockpiling weapons and spreading extremist rhetoric. Investigate their intentions and, if necessary, dismantle their operation before their actions escalate and threaten the city.\n\nPRIVATE GM DOSSIER (never reveal to the player)\n\nFixed spatial layout:\nLower hillside path -> switchback ascent -> two-level terraced encampment. The\nupper terrace holds the tarp chapel, leader tent and main gathering. A lower\nterrace contains supplies, two parked vehicles and a locked crate shelter. A\nnarrow central stair and a longer outer path connect the terraces. The lower\nterrace has the only practical vehicle exit, descending toward the city-side\nroad.\n\nStanding roles, positions, and routines:\nTwo lookouts cover the outer path and upper terrace. The leader stays near the\nupper gathering. Three armed organizers guard packed incendiaries on the lower\nterrace. One organizer carries the locked crate-shelter key; another is the\ndriver of the vehicle nearest the exit and carries its keys. Devotees move\nbetween prayer and water points but do not control the vehicles.\n\nPersistent causal rules:\nThe organizers intend to load the packed incendiaries into the vehicle nearest\nthe exit and take them to a secular community hall after the final chant. A\ncandle-wax trail on the outer path marks prior movement between the gathering\nand the lower staging area. An alarm causes the organizers to accelerate\ndeparture; it does not create new attackers or routes.\n\nResolution boundaries:\nFull success establishes the planned target, prevents the armed organizers\nfrom escaping with the incendiaries, and preserves decisive evidence. Partial\nsuccess stops the departure but loses the target link, or preserves decisive\ntarget evidence while one or more organizers or prepared materials get away.\nFailure occurs if the fixed attack party gets beyond practical interception on\nthe city-side road with the prepared incendiaries while no decisive target\nevidence has been preserved.\n\nPressure and continuity:\nTrack the final chant, lower-terrace custody, both inter-terrace routes, the\nvehicles and lookout awareness. The upper congregation can become frightened\nor defensive without becoming an additional armed force.\n\nFIXED MISSION FACTS\n\nPrepared situation:\nThe visible religious gathering occupies the upper terrace, while the\noperational staging is below beside the vehicles. Candle-wax drips along the\nlonger outer path point toward the lower cache without proving who carried it.\n\nObjective, evidence, custody, and decisive placement:\n- Packed incendiaries on the lower terrace are intended for an attack on a\n  secular community hall after the final chant.\n- The target note remains inside the locked crate shelter beside the prepared\n  materials.\n\nWhat must be accomplished:\nPrevent the fixed armed departure and preserve the evidence tying the\nlower-terrace staging to the intended target.\n\nUseful lead or workable leverage:\nCandle-wax drops continue away from the upper gathering and down the outer\npath toward the lower terrace.\n\nLive danger:\nThe lower terrace can be isolated from the upper gathering if the armed\norganizers control both the central stair and the lower end of the outer path,\nwhile the vehicle exit remains their outbound route.\n\nMisleading, partial, or irrelevant elements:\n- The upper leader tent contains rhetoric and membership lists but not the\n  target note.\n\nBinding spatial, custody, and parallel conditions:\nThe central stair is directly visible from the upper gathering, while scrub\nhides part of the longer outer path. The lower vehicle area remains open from\nthe lookout side.\n\nLater consequences; apply only when their cause occurs:\n- When the final chant ends, the three armed organizers begin loading the\n  packed materials into the designated vehicle and then drive out toward the\n  city-side road.\n- If an alarm reaches the lower terrace first, they begin that departure early\n  rather than waiting for the chant.\n\nOperational facts:\n- The packed materials remain on the lower terrace and the target note begins\n  inside the locked crate shelter; the designated organizer retains the shelter\n  key until physically moved or taken.\n- The designated driver retains the lead-vehicle keys until physically moved\n  or taken. The second parked vehicle begins unused.\n- The central stair and outer path are the only foot connections between\n  terraces.",
