      "MISSION 1: Glyfada Beach Bar Drug Deal\nCategory: Surveillance & Stakeouts\n\nPublic description to show in mission selection:\nDisrupt a drug deal at a beachside bar in Glyfada.\n\nPRIVATE GM DOSSIER (never reveal to the player)\n\nFixed spatial layout:\nThe main bar counter faces the public seating area, while a narrow side gate beside the DJ booth opens directly onto a short curbside pickup lane. The service corridor and sand lockers remain inside the venue but play no role in the exchange. A dark hatchback uses the curbside lane for only a brief stop.\n\nStanding roles, positions, and routines:\nThe seller waits at the service-counter end with the drug packet. The buyer drives the dark hatchback and carries the payment envelope. The DJ knows only a coded dedication requested by the seller and does not know its criminal meaning. A bouncer watches the side gate as part of ordinary crowd control.\n\nPersistent causal rules:\nA specific DJ dedication is the prearranged cue. When it is spoken, the buyer enters the curbside lane and waits for two minutes. The seller walks to the side gate, hands the packet through the passenger window and receives the envelope. If the two-minute window closes without contact, the buyer drives away and the deal is abandoned for the night.\n\nResolution boundaries:\nFull success documents the curbside exchange, or deliberately prevents it while both principals, packet and payment are still clearly linked. Partial success identifies the buyer vehicle and seller but cannot prove the transfer/payment chain, or preserves the packet while the buyer escapes unidentified. Failure lets the buyer leave after the two-minute window or after a completed transfer without sufficient evidence to establish the buyer/seller transaction.\n\nPressure and continuity:\nTrack DJ set order, seller position, bouncer attention, hatchback arrival, two-minute stop and packet/payment custody.\n\nFIXED MISSION FACTS\n\nPrepared situation:\nThe seller already has the packet at the service-counter end. The buyer has not yet arrived. The coded dedication is written on the DJ's request slip among ordinary song requests.\n\nObjective, evidence, custody, and decisive placement:\n- The seller starts with the packet.\n- The dark hatchback arrives only after the coded dedication.\n- The buyer keeps the payment envelope until the side-gate exchange.\n\nWhat must be accomplished:\nDisrupt or document the brief vehicle handoff at the beach bar and establish the buyer and seller behind it.\n\nUseful lead or workable leverage:\nThe coded dedication on the DJ request slip matches a phrase written on the seller's table receipt.\n\nLive danger:\nThe buyer waits exactly two minutes in the curbside lane and then leaves if the exchange has not happened.\n\nMisleading, partial, or irrelevant elements:\n- Cash left on public tables is ordinary bar payment and has no role in the deal.\n\nBinding spatial, custody, and parallel conditions:\nA ride-hailing car stops in the same pickup lane before the coded dedication and leaves with two normal customers.\n\nLater consequences; apply only when their cause occurs:\n- The coded dedication triggers the buyer's arrival at the curbside lane.\n- The seller approaches the side gate with the packet.\n- If contact occurs, the seller hands over the packet and receives the payment envelope; the hatchback then leaves immediately into the coastal street.\n- If no contact occurs before the two-minute stop ends, the buyer leaves with the payment envelope and the seller retains the packet; the deal is abandoned for the night.\n- Departure does not erase evidence already preserved.",
