      "MISSION 1: Varkiza Hotel Arms Deal\nCategory: Surveillance & Stakeouts\n\nPublic description to show in mission selection:\nIntelligence reports an illegal arms deal going down at a luxurious Varkiza\nhotel. Conduct surveillance, identify the key players, and gather evidence.\nDecide whether to simply report your findings or intervene to disrupt the\nexchange and secure the weapons.\n\nPRIVATE GM DOSSIER (never reveal to the player)\nFixed spatial layout:\nA sea-facing suite floor sits above the main hotel lobby. Two adjacent suites share a short private corridor reached by guest elevator and fire stair. The seller occupies the larger corner suite; the buyer has taken the neighboring suite under another name. Room-service staging is at the corridor end. The underground garage connects to the lobby by a separate elevator and has a vehicle ramp to the coastal road; there is no direct lift from the garage to the suite floor.\n\nStanding roles, positions, and routines:\nThe seller and one bodyguard remain in the corner suite. The buyer waits next door with a technical adviser. A seller courier brings the sample up from the garage in an ordinary hard case. Hotel room-service staff pass through the corridor on scheduled deliveries and know nothing about the deal. The buyer's driver waits in the buyer car in the garage and holds its ignition key.\n\nPersistent causal rules:\nSeller and buyer avoid being seen together in public. The courier brings the sample from the garage to the lobby, then by guest elevator to the seller's suite; the buyer's adviser crosses the private corridor for inspection while the buyer remains next door. Once the adviser approves, the buyer crosses for a short face-to-face payment confirmation. The same seller courier then carries the sample back by guest elevator to the lobby, transfers to the garage elevator, and hands the case to the buyer's driver in the garage. The driver then has the normal external removal route through the garage ramp to the coastal road.\n\nResolution boundaries:\nSurveillance is a Full success once both suites, the adviser crossing, the later buyer meeting and the same sample case's return toward the buyer vehicle are connected with reliable continuity; later departure does not erase that completed chain. Intervention is a Full success if the sample is secured while enough evidence remains to identify both principals. Partial success catches the courier or sample without linking the buyer, or links both principals without ever confirming the weapon case. Failure occurs only if neither a complete intelligence chain nor control of the sample is achieved before the sample/principals disperse beyond practical follow-up; exposure inside the hotel is pressure, not automatic Failure while a credible evidence or recovery route remains.\n\nPressure and continuity:\nTrack courier ascent, adviser crossing, buyer crossing, sample custody, room-service traffic and garage-driver readiness. Each movement follows the inspection sequence; ordinary corridor activity does not alter either principal's route.\n\nFIXED MISSION FACTS\n\nPrepared situation:\nThe buyer is already in the neighboring suite. The seller waits in the corner suite. The sample courier is in the garage carrying the hard case toward the lobby elevator. The buyer's driver waits in the buyer car in the garage with the ignition key. A room-service trolley is being prepared for another guest on the same floor.\n\nObjective, evidence, custody, and decisive placement:\n- The sample starts in the hard case carried by the seller courier from the garage.\n- The buyer and seller start in separate adjacent suites and do not meet until the adviser approves the sample.\n- The buyer's driver starts in the garage in the buyer car and receives the case only after inspection and payment confirmation.\n\nWhat must be accomplished:\nReconstruct the deliberately separated hotel-room exchange well enough to identify both sides, then report it or intervene without losing track of the weapon case.\n\nUseful lead or workable leverage:\nThe neighboring suites were booked minutes apart through different names but share one contact number in the hotel's internal booking notes.\n\nLive danger:\nThe short private corridor gives very little recovery time if either side notices surveillance, while innocent room-service staff can be caught in the same confined space.\n\nMisleading, partial, or irrelevant elements:\n- A hard case delivered to another floor contains a guest's musical instrument.\n- The fire stair reaches the lobby level but not the underground garage directly.\n\nBinding spatial, custody, and parallel conditions:\nRoom service reaches the suite floor just before the adviser's planned crossing. The trolley temporarily narrows the private corridor but also creates legitimate staff presence.\n\nLater consequences; apply only when their cause occurs:\n- When the sample reaches the seller suite, the adviser crosses from the buyer suite for inspection.\n- Only after the adviser returns and confirms does the buyer cross for the short payment meeting.\n- After payment confirmation, the seller courier carries the same case by guest elevator to the lobby, then by the separate garage elevator down to the buyer's driver.\n- After receiving the case, the buyer's driver loads it into the car and can leave through the garage ramp to the coastal road.\n- External case loss exists only once the buyer car gets beyond practical interception; losing sight of the case inside the hotel breaks direct continuity but does not by itself make the case irretrievable.\n\n",
