      "MISSION 1: The Bournazi Bandit\nCategory: Investigations\n\nPublic description to show in mission selection:\nRicardo \"El Ritmo\" Alvarez, a charismatic Spanish lindy hop and salsa\ninstructor with a cascade of curly hair, holds court at a popular dance club\nin Bournazi. He's adored by his students, particularly middle-aged women who\nare captivated by his charm and dance skills. However, Ricardo is a\nmanipulative con artist. He uses his seductive influence to persuade these\nwomen to steal valuables, jewelry, cash, electronics, from their own homes,\npromising them a future filled with romance and adventure. Your objective is\nto expose Ricardo's scheme and bring him to justice. You could gather evidence\nof his manipulation (recordings, testimonies from victims), disrupt his\noperation (warn potential victims, sabotage his classes), or perhaps even set\na trap using one of his own tactics against him. Consider the long-term\nconsequences of your actions; simply exposing him might not be enough to stop\nhim permanently. He could move operations, or seek revenge.\n\nPRIVATE GM DOSSIER (never reveal to the player)\n\nFixed spatial layout:\nA crowded weekend social fills a two-level dance club: street entrance ->\nlower bar and main floor -> open stair -> smaller upper dance room and smoking\nterrace. A coat alcove sits beside the stair. The terrace returns only to the\nupper room; it has no exterior stair.\n\nStanding roles, positions, and routines:\nRicardo moves between the two dance floors as host. A former student who left\nmonths ago has returned with an old phone containing two incriminating voice\nnotes. A current admirer stays close to Ricardo and interprets criticism as\njealousy. Club staff manage music and drinks but are not part of the scheme.\n\nPersistent causal rules:\nThe former student's old phone contains two separate voice notes in which\nRicardo instructs thefts using the same promise. She owns and controls the\nphone and will not surrender it permanently, though she can choose to provide\na copy or testimony. Her anger at Ricardo is genuine but does not falsify the\nrecordings.\n\nResolution boundaries:\nFull success requires preserving an attributable copy of the voice notes,\nobtaining testimony or corroboration strong enough to survive a jealousy\nclaim, and disrupting Ricardo's access to current victims. Partial success\npreserves the recordings without enough corroboration, or convinces one\ncurrent student to leave while Ricardo's broader influence survives. Failure\nrequires the former student to be publicly discredited or driven away before\nany attributable copy or corroborating testimony is preserved and without any\ncurrent victim meaningfully disengaging from Ricardo, leaving him free to\ncontinue or relocate the scheme.\n\nPressure and continuity:\nTrack the former student's willingness to stay, Ricardo's movement between\nfloors, crowd sentiment and whether the current admirer realizes who the\nreturning woman is. No automatic confrontation occurs merely because evidence\nis discussed.\n\nFIXED MISSION FACTS\n\nPrepared situation:\nA former victim has come back to the club carrying the strongest testimony\nyet: her old phone still holds two voice notes ordering separate thefts. She\nwants Ricardo exposed but is angry enough to make herself easy to dismiss as a\njealous ex-student.\n\nObjective, evidence, custody, and decisive placement:\n- The former student retains custody of the old phone containing two\n  incriminating voice notes.\n- The recordings become much stronger when matched to the dates on Ricardo's\n  private-lesson schedule or another willing victim's testimony.\n\nWhat must be accomplished:\nTurn the former victim's evidence into a credible case, protect her from being\nsocially isolated, and meaningfully disrupt Ricardo's access to current\nvictims.\n\nUseful lead or workable leverage:\nThe dates spoken in the voice notes match two gaps in the private-lesson\nschedule posted beside the upper-room stair.\n\nLive danger:\nA loud accusation without corroboration lets Ricardo frame the former student\nas vindictive and can push undecided students back toward him.\n\nMisleading, partial, or irrelevant elements:\n- The former student does want personal revenge, but the recordings remain\n  genuine.\n- Ordinary flirtation among dancers has no evidentiary value.\n\nBinding spatial, custody, and parallel conditions:\nThe former student waits alone at an upper-room side table with the phone in\nher bag. Ricardo is hosting on the lower floor, and the current admirer has\nnot noticed her arrival.\n\nLater consequences; apply only when their cause occurs:\n- If the former student is publicly mocked or cornered, she leaves through\n  the street entrance with her phone and refuses further contact that night.\n- If Ricardo realizes the recordings exist, he begins telling students that\n  the former victim fabricated them but cannot erase the phone remotely.\n",
