      "MISSION 1: The Bournazi Bandit\nCategory: Investigations\n\nPublic description to show in mission selection:\nRicardo \"El Ritmo\" Alvarez, a charismatic Spanish lindy hop and salsa\ninstructor with a cascade of curly hair, holds court at a popular dance club\nin Bournazi. He's adored by his students, particularly middle-aged women who\nare captivated by his charm and dance skills. However, Ricardo is a\nmanipulative con artist. He uses his seductive influence to persuade these\nwomen to steal valuables, jewelry, cash, electronics, from their own homes,\npromising them a future filled with romance and adventure. Your objective is\nto expose Ricardo's scheme and bring him to justice. You could gather evidence\nof his manipulation (recordings, testimonies from victims), disrupt his\noperation (warn potential victims, sabotage his classes), or perhaps even set\na trap using one of his own tactics against him. Consider the long-term\nconsequences of your actions; simply exposing him might not be enough to stop\nhim permanently. He could move operations, or seek revenge.\n\nPRIVATE GM DOSSIER (never reveal to the player)\n\nFixed spatial layout:\nAn evening class at the Bournazi club is followed by an ordinary route through\nnearby streets: club entrance -> dance floor -> changing corner -> pavement.\nThe targeted student's home lies a short taxi ride away; a side street beside\nthe club is Ricardo's planned return handoff point. No shortcut connects the\nhome and club.\n\nStanding roles, positions, and routines:\nRicardo teaches the class and gives one student a private-lesson card before\nshe leaves. The student believes she is taking valuables from her own\nhousehold for a shared future. Ricardo stays at the club until closing and\nexpects her to return to the side street. Other students remain unaware.\n\nPersistent causal rules:\nThe reverse of the private-lesson card carries the home address and a short\nlist of targeted items in Ricardo's handwriting. The student's phone contains\nthe romantic message that explains the list. The theft has not happened at the\nstart; stopping the student protects property but does not by itself expose\nRicardo.\n\nResolution boundaries:\nFull success requires preventing or credibly documenting the planned theft in\na way that preserves the victim's dignity, securing attributable proof from\nthe lesson card, message or testimony, and leaving Ricardo unable simply to\nrepeat the tactic. Partial success prevents the theft with only weak\nattribution, or preserves the card/message after property has already been\ntaken but before the scheme is fully exposed. Failure requires the listed\nproperty to be handed to Ricardo with no attributable copy, testimony or\nequivalent proof preserved, leaving the student blamed or still under his\ncontrol.\n\nPressure and continuity:\nTrack class ending, the student's taxi departure, her arrival at home, custody\nof the lesson card and valuables, and Ricardo waiting near the club side\nstreet. Time follows the actual travel route.\n\nFIXED MISSION FACTS\n\nPrepared situation:\nTonight's theft has not yet occurred. Ricardo has written the target address\nand items on the back of a private-lesson card and expects the student to go\nhome, collect them and return for a discreet side-street handoff.\n\nObjective, evidence, custody, and decisive placement:\n- The private-lesson card carries Ricardo's handwritten address and item\n  list.\n- The targeted student starts at the club and has not yet taken the\n  valuables from home.\n\nWhat must be accomplished:\nStop or expose the planned theft with attributable evidence while keeping the\nmanipulated student from being reduced to the apparent offender.\n\nUseful lead or workable leverage:\nThe student's taxi app is already open to her home address even though she\nnormally stays for the post-class social.\n\nLive danger:\nOnce she reaches home, the student can take the listed property and return it\nto Ricardo before anyone at the club notices.\n\nMisleading, partial, or irrelevant elements:\n- The club cashbox and Ricardo's lesson fees are legitimate.\n- A side-street parked scooter belongs to a nearby takeaway shop and has no\n  role in the handoff.\n\nBinding spatial, custody, and parallel conditions:\nThe class is in its final teaching block. The student keeps the folded lesson\ncard in her phone case, Ricardo is on the dance floor, and her taxi has not\nbeen requested yet.\n\nLater consequences; apply only when their cause occurs:\n- If she is still at the club when class ends, the student requests an\n  ordinary taxi and travels to the fixed home address.\n- If she reaches home with Ricardo's plan intact, she takes the listed\n  property, requests another ordinary taxi back to the club side street, and\n  physically hands the property to Ricardo if neither person has been\n  redirected.\n",
