      "MISSION 1: Kifisia Politician Affair\nCategory: Investigations\n\nPublic description to show in mission selection:\nUncover the affair of a powerful politician in Kifisia, navigating high society events and private gatherings. Decide whether to expose the affair for leverage or protect it to gain the politician's favor for future benefits.\n\nPRIVATE GM DOSSIER (never reveal to the player)\n\nFixed spatial layout:\nPrivate gathering in a modern Kifisia penthouse: building foyer -> lift landing -> open living room -> balcony -> compact study alcove -> service corridor and basement parking. The study alcove has no separate exterior access. Guests use the main lift; household staff use the service corridor to the same foyer.\n\nStanding roles, positions, and routines:\nThe politician hosts a small donor-and-friends gathering. The lover, a communications adviser, stays near the balcony and study alcove. A senior aide circulates with a guest list and quietly notes who spends time with whom. A cleaner finishes work early; the building porter remains downstairs.\n\nPersistent causal rules:\nThe affair is real. The lover wants to end it and has saved a voice message from the politician on a dedicated phone left charging in the study alcove. A small handwritten slip beside the charger carries the address of a private meeting property. The senior aide knows the phone matters but does not know its unlock code. The same unusual address circulates in guest gossip, but the gossip and paper slip do not substitute for the voice evidence.\n\nResolution boundaries:\n  Full success obtains credible affair proof from the dedicated phone and enough corroborating social context to distinguish exposure from mere gossip, leaving the expose-or-protect choice open. Partial success gets the address pattern or a credible relationship observation without the voice evidence, or preserves a copy of the phone evidence after social access collapses. Failure requires the phone to leave the building beyond practical follow-up with no attributable copy of the voice message, no credible relationship observation and no usable address-context link preserved.\n\n  Pressure and continuity:\n  Track the aide's guest observations, the lover's decision to leave early, access to the study alcove and the charging phone's custody. If the aide reacts first, the relevant barrier is the aide's direct physical custody of the briefcase, not an invented key puzzle. Social suspicion changes who watches the player; it does not create new evidence.\n\n  Prepared situation:\nSeveral guests repeat the same property address as harmless gossip, and a handwritten slip beside the charging phone carries that address. Only the lover's saved voice message turns the surrounding pattern into direct affair proof. The lover intends to take the phone and leave early after a tense exchange with the politician.\n\nObjective, evidence, custody, and decisive placement:\n- The dedicated phone starts charging in the study alcove.\n- It holds a saved voice message from the politician; a separate handwritten slip beside the charger carries the same property address heard in guest conversation.\n- The lover knows the unlock code and intends to leave with the phone.\n\nWhat must be accomplished:\nEstablish the affair through the phone and corroborating social context, then preserve the player's ability to expose the secret or protect it for political favor.\n\nUseful lead or workable leverage:\nThe same unusual property address appears in two guest conversations and on the handwritten slip beside the charging phone.\n\nLive danger:\nThe senior aide records the player's social movements and can move the phone into secure custody once the study alcove attracts attention.\n\nMisleading, partial, or irrelevant elements:\n- Most guest gossip concerns ordinary donor rivalries.\n- A locked decorative box in the living room contains jewelry only.\n\nBinding spatial, custody, and parallel conditions:\nThe penthouse gathering is in full flow. The dedicated phone is charging in the study alcove, the lover is on the balcony, and the senior aide circulates through the living room with the guest list.\n\nLater consequences; apply only when their cause occurs:\n  - After the tense balcony exchange, if the phone is still in the study alcove and the lover has not already reached it, the lover returns for it.\n  - If the aide notices repeated attention to the alcove before the lover secures the phone, the aide places the phone inside a personal document briefcase, closes it and keeps the briefcase with him.\n  - At departure, whoever holds the phone uses the main lift. Phone contents already copied remain secured; the physical phone is externally lost only once its holder gets beyond practical follow-up outside the building.\n\n  ",
