      "MISSION 1: Palaio Faliro New Age Tech Cult\nCategory: Cyber & High-Tech Operations\n\nPublic description to show in mission selection:\nDisrupt a new age cult in Palaio Faliro that uses modern technology to control and\nmanipulate its followers. Hack their systems and expose their deceptive practices.\n\nPRIVATE GM DOSSIER (never reveal to the player)\n\nFixed spatial layout:\nThe cult's physical headquarters is a sparse apartment-office used for remote 'distance\nalignment'. A front salon contains a small audience and donation desk. A soundproof\nbroadcast room holds the leader, cameras and a voice-processing console. A locked network\ncloset contains the campaign scheduler and message archive. Across two ordinary street\nblocks, a rented retreat flat houses one follower undergoing an enforced isolation day; the\nflat has a normal building entrance and balcony but no secret connection to headquarters. A\ntrusted relative waits at a nearby cafe and will approach only if contacted or if the\nfollower leaves voluntarily.\n\nStanding roles, positions, and routines:\nThe leader broadcasts personalized guidance from headquarters. A voice technician operates\ncloned 'guide' voices generated from recorded mentors and deceased relatives. A community\nmanager runs the scheduler that sends timed check-ins, shame messages and contact\nrestrictions. Two loyal followers watch the salon feed. The isolated follower believes a\ndead relative is speaking through the app but has recently begun to doubt it.\n\nPersistent causal rules:\nThe cult's control is distributed rather than room-bound. The scheduler combines follower\nprofiles with voice synthesis to send coercive messages at predetermined intervals. The\nvoice model itself is generic; the evidence of deception lies in the message archive, source\nrecordings and scheduling rules that staff knowingly present as supernatural contact. If a\ncredible systems breach is detected before that pairing is preserved, the community manager\ncan use the scheduler console to purge the current campaign's source-to-message pairing; the\ngeneric recordings remain, but the decisive authored link is lost. The nearby follower's\napartment devices obey ordinary user settings; staff have no remote control over physical\ndoor locks.\n\nResolution boundaries:\nFull success preserves the source-to-message proof, disables the active coercive campaign in\na durable way, and gives the isolated follower credible information and a voluntary route to\noutside support. Partial success stops the campaign or secures the paired evidence while the\nother remains intact, or secures both technical goals while the follower remains undecided\nbut still free to contact support. Failure requires the final synthetic message to succeed\nin extending the follower's isolation while the coercive campaign remains active without\ncredible proof, or the community manager to purge the decisive source-to-message pairing\nbefore it is preserved while the scheduler remains capable of continuing the campaign.\n\nPressure and continuity:\nTrack broadcast phase, scheduler state, archive custody, the isolated follower's next\nscheduled message and trust at both locations. Travel between headquarters and the retreat\nflat costs ordinary elapsed time; events at the unattended node continue only according to\nthe fixed schedule and motives.\n\nFIXED MISSION FACTS\n\nPrepared situation:\nTonight's broadcast culminates in a synthetic message using the isolated follower's deceased\nsister's voice. The message will instruct the follower to cut contact with the relative\nwaiting nearby and extend isolation for another week. The community manager has the source\nrecording and generated message paired in the scheduler because the final transmission has\nnot yet fired.\n\nObjective, evidence, custody, and decisive placement:\n- The network closet holds the campaign scheduler, message archive and the paired source recording/generated message for the isolated follower.\n- The leader and voice technician remain in the broadcast room; neither carries the decisive archive.\n- The isolated follower is in the rented retreat flat with their own phone. The relative waits at the nearby cafe and has no access to the headquarters system.\n\nWhat must be accomplished:\nSecure credible evidence that the supposedly supernatural messages are synthesized from\nrecorded voices and profiles, stop the active coercive campaign from continuing, and let the\nisolated follower make an informed choice about leaving or contacting outside support.\n\nUseful lead or workable leverage:\nA rehearsal monitor in the broadcast room plays the dead sister's voice twice with two\ndifferent generated endings while the leader discusses which version will produce more\ncompliance.\n\nLive danger:\nA badly timed confrontation can cause the isolated follower to receive the final\nmanipulative message first and interpret outside contact as the predicted 'test' the cult\nwarned about.\n\nMisleading, partial, or irrelevant elements:\n- The salon's crystal-covered antenna is decorative and carries no network traffic.\n- A locked donation drawer contains receipts and cash but no follower-control records.\n\nBinding spatial, custody, and parallel conditions:\nThe broadcast has not started. The isolated follower has received two earlier check-ins and\nis reading the third; the community manager is at the salon desk and the network closet is\nlocked but unattended.\n\nLater consequences; apply only when their cause occurs:\n- At the scheduled transmission time, the final synthetic message is sent if the scheduler remains active.\n- If the message fires, the isolated follower follows its instruction to silence outside contacts unless persuaded by evidence or their own established doubts; no supernatural compulsion is involved.\n- If the scheduler is disabled but the paired archive is not preserved, the cult can deny the voice source and later build a new campaign from the remaining recordings. If a credible breach is detected before the pairing is preserved, the community manager uses the scheduler console if already in the closet, or returns there if elsewhere, to purge the current pairing.\n\n",
