      "MISSION 1: Psyri Foot Chase\n  Category: Escort & Extraction\n\n  Public description to show in mission selection:\n  Escort a valuable informant through the dense, labyrinthine streets and alleys of Psyri. This is mainly a desperate foot chase to evade determined pursuers, where quick thinking and using the urban environment, possibly with some parkour-style maneuvers to overcome obstacles, will be key to reaching the safe zone.\n\n  PRIVATE GM DOSSIER (never reveal to the player)\n\n  Fixed spatial layout:\n  A zigzag route crosses a pedestrian lane, a small square, a service alley behind bars, and an exterior stair that drops to a commercial loading bay. The loading bay is the fixed extraction point. A secure contact car will arrive there from the larger street at a known time, wait exactly two minutes, then depart. A decorative passage marked as an arcade ends at locked storage doors and does not reach the bay.\n\n  Standing roles, positions, and routines:\n  The informant can run but is tiring. Two pursuers follow directly; a third pursuer has gone ahead toward the loading bay after hearing the destination from a compromised phone call, but does not know the exact arrival minute. The contact driver is independent, follows the prearranged schedule and will not circle back after departure.\n\n  Resolution boundaries:\n  Full success gets the informant into the contact car during its two-minute loading-bay window without a pursuer entering the vehicle. Partial success reaches the bay after exposing the driver/location but still extracts. Failure misses the finite car window with no alternate extraction already established, or the pursuers capture the informant before boarding.\n\n  Pressure and continuity:\n  Track real route progress, informant stamina, the contact car's scheduled arrival/departure and the ahead pursuer's movement toward the bay. The driver arrives on schedule whether or not the player can see it and leaves two minutes later unless physically prevented by a concrete event.\n\n  FIXED MISSION FACTS\n\n  Prepared situation:\n  The safe zone is not a static room but a prearranged two-minute pickup at a commercial loading bay. The opposition learned the general destination but not the exact timing, turning the chase into a race against both the clock and an interceptor approaching from ahead.\n\n  Objective, evidence, custody, and decisive placement:\n  - The contact car is off-map at start and is already committed to arrive at the loading bay at the prearranged minute.\n- The ahead pursuer begins two blocks from the loading bay and knows only that an extraction is expected there.\n- The two trailing pursuers begin behind the player and informant on the pedestrian lane.\n- The informant's testimony remains the valuable asset; no document cache at the bay substitutes for them.\n\n  What must be accomplished:\n  Keep the informant moving through the physically connected route and deliver them into the scheduled contact car before the finite pickup window closes.\n\n  Useful lead or workable leverage:\n  A loading-bay clock visible from the service alley lets the player compare actual time with the informant's remembered pickup minute.\n\n  Live danger:\n  Arriving too early can expose the loading bay to the ahead pursuer; arriving too late ends the only prearranged extraction.\n\n  Misleading, partial, or irrelevant elements:\n  - A black sedan idling on another street is a private-hire pickup, not the contact car.\n- The locked decorative arcade cannot be forced into an equivalent route without a real means to breach it.\n\n  Binding spatial, custody, and parallel conditions:\n  The contact car is still several minutes from its scheduled arrival. The trailing pursuers are close enough to hear footsteps behind, while the ahead pursuer is moving toward the loading-bay block from another direction.\n\n  Later consequences; apply only when their cause occurs:\n  - Before arrival the contact car remains off-map; once it reaches the loading bay, its two-minute wait runs continuously and it departs at the end if nobody boards.\n- If the ahead pursuer sees the car arrive, they commit to the loading bay and can signal the trailing pursuers only from that established observation.",
