      "MISSION 1: Strip Club Extraction on Syngrou Avenue\nCategory: Escort & Extraction\n\nPublic description to show in mission selection:\nExtract a key witness from a strip club on Syngrou Avenue while avoiding the\ncriminal organization hunting them. The key witness is a stripper.\n\nPRIVATE GM DOSSIER (never reveal to the player)\n\nFixed spatial layout:\nAvenue entrance -> modern main floor with bar and stage -> mezzanine VIP\nlevel. A controlled door beside the stage descends to a lower dressing room\nand service-lift lobby. The service lift reaches an underground garage with\none vehicle ramp to a side street. The main entrance remains the only\npedestrian street exit above ground.\n\nStanding roles, positions, and routines:\nThe witness begins in the lower dressing room before the final song. One\norganization driver waits off-site until the final cue, then parks in the\nunderground garage facing the vehicle ramp. A club security employee watches\nthe controlled door for ordinary access rules and has no knowledge of the\nwitness hunt.\n\nPersistent causal rules:\nAt the final song cue the witness finishes work and the organization driver\nenters the garage. The driver watches the ramp and parked vehicles, not the\nservice-lift doors until someone emerges. The controlled backstage stair to the main floor and the service lift remain\nthe only established routes from the dressing level.\n\nResolution boundaries:\nFull success gets the willing witness from the dressing level to secure onward\ncover without the organization driver regaining custody. Partial success\nescapes the club but exposes the witness's route or leaves the evidence phone\nbehind. Failure ends with the witness intercepted and retaken before secure\nonward cover.\n\nPressure and continuity:\nTrack the final-song cue, driver position, controlled backstage door, service-\nlift state, witness trust and the chosen onward route. Before the cue the\ndriver is not in the garage.\n\nFIXED MISSION FACTS\n\nPrepared situation:\nThe lower dressing area offers a discreet service lift, but the organization's\npickup plan uses the same garage after the final song. The front exit remains\nviable through the public floor, trading concealment for exposure. The witness\nkeeps a worn popular-mathematics paperback and pencil in the dressing room and\nreads it between sets, a private hobby little remarked on at work.\n\nObjective, evidence, custody, and decisive placement:\n- The witness begins in the lower dressing room with the evidence phone inside\n  a street bag.\n- The service lift reaches the underground garage; the main-floor route\n  reaches the avenue.\n\nWhat must be accomplished:\nExtract the witness willingly through either established route and reach\nsecure onward movement before the organization retakes them.\n\nUseful lead or workable leverage:\nA printed staff notice lists the service lift as the only connection between\nthe lower dressing level and the garage.\n\nLive danger:\nAt the final song cue the organization's driver takes a fixed position in the\ngarage and watches the vehicle ramp.\n\nMisleading, partial, or irrelevant elements:\n- The mezzanine VIP level has no direct exit to the street or garage.\n- An unrelated parked car near the lift belongs to club staff.\n\nBinding spatial, custody, and parallel conditions:\nThe service lift is at the dressing level and its doors are closed. The\norganization driver has not yet entered the garage.\n\nLater consequences; apply only when their cause occurs:\n- At the final song cue the organization driver enters the garage, parks\n  facing the ramp and stays there until alerted or physically displaced.\n- Emerging from the service lift into the driver's clear view reveals the\n  witness immediately.\n\nOperational facts:\n- The witness's street bag and evidence phone remain in the dressing room\n  until moved.\n- The service lift reaches only the dressing level, garage and main-floor\n  service lobby.",
