      "MISSION 1: Anavyssos Seafront Estate Hostage Crisis\nCategory: Rescue Missions\n\nPublic description to show in mission selection:\nRescue hostages from an armed group holding a private seafront estate near\nAnavyssos.\n\nPRIVATE GM DOSSIER (never reveal to the player)\n\nFixed spatial layout:\nThe estate is hosting a private celebration across the main salon, covered\ndining terrace and guesthouse. A service basement beneath the main villa\ncontains laundry, storage and a staff break room; stairs from the kitchen\nconnect it to the salon level. The detached guesthouse stands across the\ngarden and has its own single door. The road gate and beach path are both\nvisible from parts of the garden.\n\nStanding roles, positions, and routines:\nThe armed group seized the celebration mid-evening. Three captors hold guests\nin the main salon, and one of them handles the outside negotiation; one holds\nestate staff in the service basement; two guard a politically valuable guest\nin the detached guesthouse. A frightened junior captor moves food and water\nbetween main house and guesthouse and dislikes the threat to kill staff. A\nhired escape sedan with a waiting driver remains outside the road gate until\nthe salon negotiator signals it in.\n\nPersistent causal rules:\nThe captors want to exchange the valuable guest for safe departure, while the\nbasement staff are retained as labor and insurance. The junior captor follows\ndelivery orders along the garden route and can become a communication seam but\nwill not spontaneously free anyone. The guesthouse group plans to move its\nhostage only after the salon negotiator signals the waiting sedan through the\nroad gate.\n\nResolution boundaries:\nFull success frees the salon guests, basement staff and guesthouse hostage\nwhile ending the active threat. Partial success saves the majority but the\nvaluable guest is removed, or frees all civilians while the basement captor\nescapes armed and mobile. Failure results in hostage killing or ends with\nmultiple hostage zones still under armed control.\n\nPressure and continuity:\nTrack vehicle approach, junior-captor loyalty, basement access, guesthouse\ncustody and awareness between zones. Separate buildings remain separate\ntactical problems even though the armed group shares radios.\n\nFIXED MISSION FACTS\n\nPrepared situation:\nThe hostages are distributed across three zones created by the celebration\nlayout. The junior captor is already making supervised supply trips through\nthe garden.\n\nObjective, evidence, custody, and decisive placement:\n- Celebration guests start in the main salon.\n- Estate staff start confined in the service-basement break room.\n- The politically valuable guest starts in the detached guesthouse with two\ncaptors.\n\nWhat must be accomplished:\nSecure all three hostage zones and prevent the guesthouse hostage from being\ndriven out through the road gate before reprisals spread between buildings.\n\nUseful lead or workable leverage:\nA basement staff member knows the junior captor leaves the guesthouse door\nunlatched during supply trips because both hands are occupied.\n\nLive danger:\nThe salon negotiator's signal bringing the escape sedan through the road gate\nbegins the guesthouse hostage transfer and raises tension in the main salon.\n\nMisleading, partial, or irrelevant elements:\n- The celebration fireworks stored near the garden shed are legal event\nsupplies and are not part of the captors' plan.\n\nBinding spatial, custody, and parallel conditions:\nA food trolley follows the same garden paving between kitchen and guesthouse,\nleaving a clear wheel track after spilled water.\n\nLater consequences; apply only when their cause occurs:\n- When the salon negotiator signals the waiting driver and the sedan enters\nthrough the road gate, it stops near the guesthouse and the guesthouse captors\nprepare the valuable guest for movement. Once the hostage is loaded, the sedan\nleaves by the same road gate unless physically stopped.\n- If the junior captor is given credible proof that staff will be killed, that\ncaptor becomes willing to stop making supply runs and share what was seen.\n- If the main-salon captors learn that the basement has been lost, they move\nguests to the terrace-side end of the salon, farther from the kitchen stair.",
